# Menu Locale Overrides: Exit Animation To-Do

Investigation date: 2026-10-23. Status: open; no runtime fix implemented.

- [ ] Restore borrowed locale strings after the outgoing panel stops rendering,
  before the destination menu builds, across all affected modded menus.

## Symptom and Cause

The user observed original native labels briefly appearing in the Archipelago
menu's exit animation. Source review and Ghidra analysis show the same timing
problem in the other overridden menus: their action handlers restore strings
when navigation is requested, rather than when the outgoing panel disappears.

`RestoreLocaleString` in `DLL/Game/LocaleUtils.cpp` immediately replaces a pointer
in RVGL's shared locale table. It does not defer restoration or track animations.
Native rendering resolves menu labels from that table each frame; it does not
keep a copy of the text that was displayed before navigation.

## Affected Paths

| Menu | Current restoration point |
| --- | --- |
| Archipelago connection form | `HandleConnectionMenuAction` restores four field/action labels immediately after Back; `UpdateArchipelagoMenu` restores them immediately after starting the return transition on successful authentication. |
| Main menu's Archipelago entry | `Hook_HandleMainMenuAction` restores its label when the destination changes to another native menu; it retains the shared label when opening Archipelago. |
| Mod Settings | `HandleModOptionsMenuAction` restores its four setting labels immediately after Back. The shared title remains available for the parent Options menu. |
| Options | `Hook_HandleOptionsMenuAction` restores the Mod Settings label immediately after Back or Confirm into another native submenu. Opening Mod Settings retains its shared title label. |
| Start Race | `Hook_HandleStartRaceMenuAction` restores the borrowed Knockout row label immediately after Confirm or Back. Rebuild/selection-reset paths also restore it. |

The user's visual observation concerns Archipelago. The other affected paths
were identified from their restoration timing and the native rendering flow.

## Native Flow Confirmed in Ghidra

Addresses below are absolute addresses in the analysed executable, image base
`0x00400000`.

| Function | Address | Relevant behavior |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `UpdateMenuPanel` | `0x00546C80` | Calls panel-state update, input handling, then rendering for each display slot. |
| `HandleMenuRowInput` | `0x00546AB0` | Invokes the panel's action handler, then starts a transition if its destination changed. |
| `HandleGenericMenuAction` | `0x00546CF0` | Back/Confirm set the destination panel without immediately replacing the displayed panel. |
| `Menu_ActivateDisplaySlot` | `0x00544E30` | Configures the outgoing animation and marks the current panel as leaving. |
| `HandleMenuPanelState` | `0x00545AB0` | Advances the animation; once the outgoing phase finishes, replaces the current panel and invokes the destination builder. |
| `RenderMenuPanel` | `0x0054ACF0` | Continues drawing the current panel during its outgoing animation; resolves the title through the locale table. |
| `DrawMenuRow` | `0x00547050` | Resolves each row's numeric label ID through the current locale table on every draw. |

Restoration in an action handler therefore affects the outgoing panel's next
draw, potentially on the same frame as the navigation request.

## Required Lifecycle and Verification

Keep outgoing overrides active throughout the exit animation. Restore them when
RVGL retires the outgoing panel, before the destination builder reads or
overrides those locale entries. Preserve labels shared by a parent menu entry
and its submenu title where appropriate.

The exact hook/callback for this change remains to be selected. Waiting until
after `HandleMenuPanelState` returns can be too late: the destination builder
runs inside that function. Static labels do not need to be reapplied every frame.

Verify in RVGL that labels remain unchanged throughout outgoing animations for
Archipelago Back/success, main-menu navigation, Mod Settings Back, Options
navigation, and Start Race Confirm/Back. Also verify that destination menus see
their correct native labels, including repeated visits and language changes.
